  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Kiteretsu goes to his Chemistry Lab to perform the perfect reaction.\nIn his lab, he found NNN reagents numbered 111 to NNN. The ithi^{th}ith reagent has two properties - AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​.\n\nA reaction can be performed between the reagents iii and jjj **only if** Ai≤jA_i \\leq jAi​≤j.\n\nIf a reaction is performed between reagents iii and jjj, i⋅ji \\cdot ji⋅j amount of heat is produced. Out of this, D⋅(Bi⊕Bj)D \\cdot (B_i \\oplus B_j)D⋅(Bi​⊕Bj​) is absorbed and the rest heat is released. Here, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\n\nMore formally, in a reaction between reagents iii and jjj, the heat released is given by:\n\n\nH(i,j)=i⋅j−D⋅(Bi⊕Bj)H(i,j)= i \\cdot j - D \\cdot (B_i \\oplus B_j)H(i,j)=i⋅j−D⋅(Bi​⊕Bj​)\nFind the **maximum** possible heat which can be released in a reaction.\n\n**Note**: The input of this problem is large, so use fast input/output methods.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line will contain TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nFirst line of each test case contains two integers N,DN, DN,D.\nSecond line of each test case contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThird line of each test case contains NNN integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line, a single integer denoting the maximum possible heat that can be released in a reaction.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "2≤N≤1062 \\leq N \\leq 10^62≤N≤106",
      "1≤D≤20001 \\leq D \\leq 20001≤D≤2000",
      "(i+1)≤Ai≤N(i+1) \\leq  A_i \\leq N(i+1)≤Ai​≤N ∀\\forall∀ (1≤i&lt;N)(1 \\leq i \\lt N)(1≤i&lt;N)",
      "AN=N+1A_N=N+1AN​=N+1",
      "1≤Bi≤N1 \\leq B_i \\leq N1≤Bi​≤N",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5 2\n2 4 5 5 6\n1 3 2 2 5\n2 3\n2 3\n1 2",
        "output": "6\n-7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: Let us choose i=2i = 2i=2 and j=4j = 4j=4. Since A2≤4A_2 \\leq 4A2​≤4, a reaction can take place.\nThe heat released in this reaction is 2⋅4−2⋅(3⊕2)=8−2⋅1=62\\cdot 4 - 2\\cdot (3 \\oplus 2) = 8-2 \\cdot 1 = 62⋅4−2⋅(3⊕2)=8−2⋅1=6. It can be proven that for no other reaction, the heat released is greater than 666.\nSome other reactions can take place between (2,5)(2, 5)(2,5), (3,5)(3,5)(3,5). Note that no reaction is possible between (3,4)(3,4)(3,4) as A3≰4A_3 \\nleq 4A3​≰4.\nTest Case 222: The only possible reaction is between reagents 111 and 222. The heat released in this reaction is 1⋅2−3⋅(1⊕2)=2−3⋅3=−71 \\cdot 2 - 3\\cdot (1 \\oplus 2) = 2 - 3\\cdot 3 = -71⋅2−3⋅(1⊕2)=2−3⋅3=−7."
      }
    ]
  },
